From: System 573 MiSTer integration
Subject: [PATCH] cd_top: initialise positionInIndex to 0 for NVC time-0 safety

NVC defaults an uninitialised `integer range -524288 to 524287` to its left
bound (-524288). The concurrent savestate-export assignment

    ss_out(11)(19 downto 0) <= std_logic_vector(to_unsigned(positionInIndex, 20));

(cd_top.vhd ~2381) is evaluated at time 0 during initialisation, before any
clock edge or reset, so to_unsigned() sees -524288 and raises a FATAL
NATURAL-range error under NVC's strict numeric_std checks (ModelSim tolerates
the negative-to-unsigned conversion and the upstream sim never hit it).

This is a pure NVC-portability fix with no behavioural effect: positionInIndex
is driven synchronously thereafter, and ss_out(11) feeds only the savestate
machinery, which is disabled in the Phase-2 boot harness (save_state='0'). The
fix is offer-back-able upstream as a harmless robustness improvement.

Kept isolated under psx_patches/ and (re)applied by tools/apply_psx_patches.sh
exactly like the EXP1 widening; the submodule pointer never moves.
---
diff --git a/rtl/cd_top.vhd b/rtl/cd_top.vhd
index c1c2522..c51d936 100644
--- a/rtl/cd_top.vhd
+++ b/rtl/cd_top.vhd
@@ -299,7 +299,7 @@ architecture arch of cd_top is
    signal sectorBuffer_addrB        : std_logic_vector(9 downto 0);
    signal sectorBuffer_DataB        : std_logic_vector(31 downto 0);
       
-   signal positionInIndex           : integer range -524288 to 524287; 
+   signal positionInIndex           : integer range -524288 to 524287 := 0; 
    signal lastReadSector            : integer range 0 to 524287; 
    signal subchannelSector          : integer range 0 to 524287; 
    signal fetchCount                : integer range 0 to 588;
